          model: "1) #1 Typeface, #2 First Sentence, #3 Second Sentence, #4 Paragraph Headings, #5 Product Explanation, #6 New Features, #7 Technical Explanation, #8 Anticipate Objections, #9 Resolve Objections, #10 Gender, #11 Clarity, #12 Clichés, #13 Rhythm, #14 Service. Bally Fireball pinball: a self-diagnosing machine with plug-in boards you remove and mail in for a replacement. Sensor 770 watch: a five-year unconditional parts-and-labor warranty, with door pickup and a loaner watch while it's repaired, at JS&A's expense.\n\n2) Every buyer was worried about reliability, and competitors ignored it. The company that answered the fear best would win, so a strong service promise became the reason to buy from JS&A instead of anyone else.\n\n3) He made his customers' service problems his own and acted as each buyer's personal service rep, so they came back only to him. For a local business: own the problem after the sale, and repeat business and referrals follow."
