          model: "1) #1 Typeface, #2 First Sentence, #3 Second Sentence, #4 Paragraph Headings, #5 Product Explanation, #6 New Features, #7 Technical Explanation, #8 Anticipate Objections, #9 Resolve Objections, #10 Gender, #11 Clarity, #12 Clichés, #13 Rhythm, #14 Service, #15 Physical Facts. Examples: the weight of the bathroom scale itself, and the weight of a hand-held product shown in his hand.\n\n2) Tests tell you that something failed. The phone told him why, in the buyer's own words, at the moment of buying, including the small, “irrelevant” questions no test would surface.\n\n3) Many more. He implies they didn't call and didn't order. A missing fact is a silent leak, and the calls are only the visible part."
