        after: "PMT: “Driver's ed for motorcycles, except it takes a weekend and you get to ride.” · Explaining the clutch: “The friction zone is the motorcycle version of a stick shift's bite point.” · Trades: home inspection = “a physical for your house”; AC tune-up = “an oil change for your air conditioner”; ceramic coating = “sunscreen for your paint.”",
        body: "Each after borrows a structure the reader already understands, so they “get it” with no effort, which is Sugarman's bridge. **Landing page:** use the link in the headline, then explain it in the first paragraph, as he did with The Nose. **Sales call:** reach for an analogy whenever a prospect looks confused (“Think of it like...”). **Checks:** make sure the link's emotional baggage is positive or neutral (no crashes, crime or tragedy), and test two or three links as ad hooks to see which one the market grasps fastest."
