        body: "The before asks for the biggest commitment first and never asks again. The after makes the first commitment tiny, then uses Sugarman's on-the-phone add-on while the customer is in buying mode. **Ad copy:** one simple ask (“See open dates”), not a menu. **Landing page:** one button, one path; the add-on comes after the booking, not before. **Sales call:** after they say yes and you've taken the details, do the Spoelstra turn: “One more thing before I let you go...” **Trades:** after an HVAC install, offer the maintenance plan; after a roof, gutter guards; after a detail, a maintenance wash. Only offer what truly helps."
